==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*mey- (change)}}
From {{inh|en|enm|mutable}}, from {{der|en|fro|mutable}}, from {{der|en|la|mutabilis||liable to change}}; {{suffix|en|mutate|able}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈmjuːtəbəl/|[ˈmjuːtəbl̩]}}
* {{homophones|en|muteable}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[change|Changeable]], [[dynamic]], [[evolutive]]; inclined to [[change]], [[evolve]], [[mutate]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1531|author=w:Thomas Elyot|chapter=Of Constance or Stabilitie|title=The boke named the gouernour|url=http://ota.ox.ac.uk/text/3091.html|section=book III|page=e4v|passage=Vndoughtedly constaunce is an honourable vertue, as inconstance is reprochefull and odious. Wherfore that man whiche is '''mutable''' for euerye occasyon, muste nedes often repente hym, and in moche repentance is nat only moche foly, but also great detriment: whiche euery wyse man wyll eschue if he can.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Coriolanus|III|i|text=For the '''mutable''' ranke-ſented [[meinie|Meynie]], / Let them [[regard]] me, as I doe not flatter, / And therein behold themſelues.}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Regained|book=Samson Agonistes|page=83|lines=415–420|passage=Maſters commands come with a power reſiſtleſs / To ſuch as owe them abſolute ſubjection; / And for a life who will not change his purpoſe? / (So '''mutable''' are all the ways of men) / Yet this be ſure, in nothing to comply / Scandalous or forbidden in our Law.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1864|author=Rob S. Candlish|title=The Fatherhood of God|journal=The British and Foreign Evangelical Review|volume=XIV|location=London|publisher=James Nisbet & Co.|year_published=1865|page=748|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=iA4EAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA748|passage=It is in vain to interpose the explanation that the sonship was '''mutable.''' The Broad School do not say so ; and in so far they are consistent, for they recognise no power to produce the mutation.}}
# {{lb|en|programming|of a variable}} Having a value that is changeable during [[program]] [[execution]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2011|author=David Flanagan|title=JavaScript: The Definitive Guide
|passage=A value of a '''mutable''' type can change. Objects and arrays are '''mutable''': a JavaScript program can change the values of object properties and array elements. Numbers, booleans, null, and undefined are immutable.}}
# {{lb|en|astrology}} Being one of the signs [[Gemini]], [[Virgo]], [[Sagittarius]] and [[Pisces]], associated with [[adaptability]], [[flexibility]] and [[sympathy]].
#: {{synonyms|en|bicorporeal}}

